  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Local Level Health Systems Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Strengthening Local Level Health Systems activity strengthens local level health systems to deliver high quality and integrated public health services. Using FY 2024 funds, this activity will work closely with district and lower-level health administrators and facility managers to develop health system improvement plans and implement targeted, evidence-based health systems strengthening interventions. While this activity will have a nationwide scope, it will primarily focus on 16 geographic catchment areas where local level health systems are the weakest and/or have the capacity to be catalytic with the support of this activity&apos;s technical assistance. The activity will advance core health system strengthening principles including equity, quality, resource optimization, evidence-based decision making, adaptive management, resilience, and locally led development. The activity will support the Joint Strategic Plan Goal Three and the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective of Improving inclusive and equitable health, education, and livelihood services, especially for women, youth, and marginalized groups. The activity will advance the Indo-Pacific Strategy by working  with GoB to intensify efforts to prevent, detect, and respond to infectious diseases.FY 2024 funding will contribute to Adaptation Indirect ($2.5m), SL Indirect ($500k),Gender Equality ($1m), GBV ($340k),GBV-CEFM ($300k), GFS ($500k), Health Workforce ($850k), Cross-Cutting HSS ($4.19m),Digital Technology- Indirect ($150k), MSN ($400k),(Macronutrients ($300k of which Vit A is $200k), PGI-Indirect Digital ($800k),PGI-Indirect Health ($6m), WASH ($200k) issues.</narrative>
  </description>
